e.0001974-Champagne1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Champagne</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Meaney</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Like mother, like daughter: evidence for non-genomic transmission of parental behavior and stress responsivity.</article-title><source>Prog Brain Res</source><volume>133</volume><fpage>287</fpage><lpage>302</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11589138</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001974-Swallow1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Swallow</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Garland</surname><given-names>T</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>1998</year><article-title>Artificial selection for increased wheel-running behavior in house mice.</article-title><source>Behav Genet</source><volume>28</volume><fpage>227</fpage><lpage>237</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9670598</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001974-Girard1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Girard</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Swallow</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Koteja</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Rhodes</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Maternal-care behavior and life-history traits in house mice (<italic>Mus domesticus</italic>) artificially selected for high voluntary wheel-running activity.</article-title><source>Behav Process</source><volume>57</volume><fpage>37</fpage><lpage>50</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001974-Gammie1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gammie</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Hasen</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rhodes</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></name><name><surname>Girard</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Garland</surname><given-names>T</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Predatory aggression, but not maternal or intermale aggression, is associated with high voluntary wheel-running behavior in mice.</article-title><source>Horm Behav</source><volume>44</volume><fpage>209</fpage><lpage>221</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14609543</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001974-Gammie2"><label>25</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gammie</surname><given-names>SC</given-names></name><name><surname>Garland</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Stevenson</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Artificial selection for increased maternal defense behavior in mice.</article-title><source>Behav Genet</source><volume>36</volume><fpage>713</fpage><lpage>722</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16676225</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0001974-Brayden1"><label>26</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Brayden</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Altemeier</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name><name><surname>Tucker</surname><given-names>DD</given-names></name><name><surname>Dietrich</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Vietze</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><year>1992</year><article-title>Antecedents of child neglect in the 1st 2 years of life.</article-title><source>J Pediatr</sour